life and what I cared about,

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.667
and I built my dad's business

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.500
from a three to a 65
million dollar business

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.917
with no capital
infusion in '98 to 2003.

00:04:24.917 --> 00:04:27.166
- [Ed] Wait, he didn't make a
modest $14 million loan?

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.291
- No, no modest
$14 million loan.

00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:30.959
(laughing)

00:04:30.959 --> 00:04:32.542
But he came to America.

00:04:32.542 --> 00:04:36.166
I was born in Belarus with no
language and a hundred bucks

00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:38.250
and lived in a studio
apartment in Queens

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.166
with eight family members,
so he's very much my hero

00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:43.208
to build it up to a three
million dollar level.

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:46.583
But I did it on 

00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:49.083
digital marketing 
innovation of the time.

00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:52.125
In 1997 I had an
e-mail newsletter

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.583
that had 91 percent open rates,

00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:56.542
because nobody
was e-mail marketing,

00:04:56.542 --> 00:04:58.041
and instead of sending catalogs

00:04:58.041 --> 00:04:59.583
from Sherry-Lehmann's or Zachys,

00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:02.417
I was getting to customers
first with the hottest wines

00:05:02.417 --> 00:05:03.583
on this thing e-mail.

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:06.375
I was trying to send as many
e-mails as possible in '97,

00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:09.458
'cause I thought people would
eventually charge for it.

00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:11.667
It seemed such a great deal.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:12.667
Launching a website, e-mail--

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:13.500
(laughing)

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.625
Really!

00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:18.875
It's funny but very honestly,
if we start talking about VR,

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.458
we're gonna make a lot
of assumptions right now

00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:22.542
that are either gonna
play out or not play out

00:05:22.542 --> 00:05:24.333
in 20 to 30 year window.

00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:27.500
1996 internet was a whole
different fucking world,

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.000
and so I kept innovating.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.250
Bought the word wine on
the day Google AdWords came out

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.000
